      "problem": "Which of the following residue classes modulo $10$ contain the integer $-4?$\n\n- $[4]_{10}$\n- $[-14]_{10}$\n- $[6]_{10}$",
      "worked_solution": "We have $-4\\in [a]_{10}$ if \n\n$$\n-4≡a\\,(\\text{mod}\\,10).\n$$\n\nLet's now consider each of the given equivalence classes.\n\n- $-4\\notin [4]_{10}$ because $-4≢4\\,(\\text{mod}\\,10)$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- $-4\\in [-14]_{10}$ because $-4≡-14\\,(\\text{mod}\\,10)$ $\\,✓$\n\n- $-4\\in [6]_{10}$ because $-4≡6\\,(\\text{mod}\\,10)$ $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\".",
